  "checked": [
    "One application-global record per registered task key stores only bounded key/generation/pending metadata. It does not impersonate an account/session and contains no message, credential or remote authority.",
    "Request atomically retains a fresh caller generation as pending. Same-current-generation replay returns existing state, including prior acknowledgment. Generation creation/non-reuse and registered task admission remain caller policy.",
    "Acknowledgment updates only the exact still-pending generation. Concurrent newer requests remain pending in either transaction order; no historical generation or owned payload is overwritten.",
    "Key capacity is checked inside the same write transaction. Forty concurrent new-key requests admit exactly eight when capacity is eight; existing keys can still advance at capacity. Completed keys remain reserved.",
    "Already-cancelled mutations are rejected before DAO/IndexedDB I/O. Once transaction I/O begins, cancellation may race a durable commit; callers must recover observed generations rather than assume rollback.",
    "Pending and acknowledged states survive database close/reopen and account replacement. SQLite11 and a frozen genuine IndexedDB10 schema preserve prior stored commands/inbox while adding wake storage.",
    "44 real SQLite and42 real browser database cases plus two application DI cases, proof Kotlin compilation and static checks pass after the cancellation fix.",
    "Final checks include the application raw-store binding and six isolated Apple test wrappers. Their native execution requires the separate hosted Apple run; Linux checks do not establish Apple acceptance."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "No all-company coordinator, durable wake scheduling, FCM receive/decrypt, notifications or inline reply is connected by this raw primitive.",
